Drop the drive prefix of a source copied by cp --parents.
cp --parents appends each SOURCE to the target directory, and leading
slashes are dropped so that an absolute path lands inside it. A drive
prefix was kept, so "cp --parents c:/src/a.h inc" tried to create
"inc/c:" and failed, or with a drive-relative path such as "c:a.h"
wrote "inc/c:a.h", which Windows takes as an alternate data stream of
the file "inc/c". Drop the drive prefix as the slashes are dropped,
giving "inc/src/a.h".

---
 coreutils/cp.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/coreutils/cp.c
+++ b/coreutils/cp.c
@@ -286,7 +286,13 @@
 		if (flags & OPT_parents) {
 			char *dest_dup;
 			char *dest_dir;
+#if ENABLE_PLATFORM_MINGW32
+			/* Like leading slashes, a drive prefix isn't appended */
+			dest = concat_path_file(last,
+					*argv + (has_dos_drive_prefix(*argv) ? 2 : 0));
+#else
 			dest = concat_path_file(last, *argv);
+#endif
 			dest_dup = xstrdup(dest);
 			dest_dir = dirname(dest_dup);
 			if (bb_make_directory(dest_dir, -1, FILEUTILS_RECUR)) {
